        "id": 149632,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-10-15T22:51:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I suppose someone named Tachyon ought to have <em>some</em> feature that violates causality!</p>\n<p>You’re right, phantaskippy, it does say “and.” I was thinking it’d work like similarly worded cards that say “do x, then do y.” Maybe a more unambiguous way to word it would have been, “If Tachyon would be dealt damage, you may destroy this card. When this card is destroyed, redirect the damage to a target of your choice.”</p>\n<p>I’m still kind of curious how this discussion pans out.</p>",
