        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "I suppose someone named Tachyon ought to have *some* feature that violates causality! \r\n\r\nYou're right, phantaskippy, it does say \"and.\" I was thinking it'd work like similarly worded cards that say \"do x, then do y.\" Maybe a more unambiguous way to word it would have been, \"If Tachyon would be dealt damage, you may destroy this card. When this card is destroyed, redirect the damage to a target of your choice.\"\r\n\r\nI'm still kind of curious how this discussion pans out.",
