      {
        "id": 149635,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-10-16T01:57:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Alacritous works because the destruction is \"if you do, destroy this card.\" &nbsp;It won't trigger until the effect finishes, because until then you haven't \"used a power.\" Since the effect of Alacritous' Accompany effect is to grant you another power, it isn't finished until the power it grants is finished, and if that power grants a card play that grants a power. . . &nbsp;You get the idea. &nbsp;The whole chain has to finish before the destruction is triggered.</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:28:08.692Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
