        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Alacritous works because the destruction is &quot;if you do, destroy this card.&quot; &nbsp;It won&#39;t trigger until the effect finishes, because until then you haven&#39;t &quot;used a power.&quot; Since the effect of Alacritous&#39; Accompany effect is to grant you another power, it isn&#39;t finished until the power it grants is finished, and if that power grants a card play that grants a power. . . &nbsp;You get the idea. &nbsp;The whole chain has to finish before the destruction is triggered.</p>",
